  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-25T20:33:09.236Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use VRChat for long periods of time in my Vive Pro headset.  As I continue to use, I noticed that it starts \"slowing down\" and it is happening every time I launch the app.  A quick fix is to restart it, but I believe something isn't closing and every time it is accessed and needs to close up, it does not.  Symptoms start to appear: loading screens slow down, fade-in is slower than normal and music studders as it fades in.  Initializing worlds take longer to build.  Every time a new user enters the instance or when I walk to the mirror and it is needed to be accessed, the app would freeze a bit.  Finally the avatars won't load and come up with a robot \"error\" one, and when I try to select \"show avatar\" in the menu, it continuously loads in an infinite loop until I tell to use safety settings.  I hop worlds a lot and I see this happening.  I'm on 3-6 hours to see it slow down.",
